WEBVTT

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.549
Previously on Supernatural 22 years ago

00:00:22.584 --> 00:00:23.667
Sammy.

00:00:24.191 --> 00:00:26.081
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:26.116 --> 00:00:26.990
Go!

00:00:27.025 --> 00:00:29.544
Their mother Mysteriously died

00:00:29.809 --> 00:00:31.982
Now two brothers...
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:34.267
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:34.302 --> 00:00:36.518
Are on a quest to find their father

00:00:37.464 --> 00:00:38.498
This is dad's book.

00:00:38.533 --> 00:00:40.711
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:42.762
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:42.797 --> 00:00:44.490
The family business.

00:00:44.652 --> 00:00:45.898
I got to find dad.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:48.472
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:07.222 --> 00:01:10.288
Where have you got those amp
up to? A hundred thousand volts.

00:01:10.438 --> 00:01:13.091
Damn. Yeah, I want this raw
head extra freaking crispy.

00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:15.745
Now, remember you only get
one shot with these things.

00:01:16.226 --> 00:01:18.188
So make it count.

00:01:50.989 --> 00:01:52.014
On three.

00:01:52.887 --> 00:01:53.955
One.

00:01:54.444 --> 00:01:55.762
Two.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:57.474
Three.

00:02:01.151 --> 00:02:02.738
Is it still here?

00:02:02.773 --> 00:02:03.888
Okay.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.803
Okay, hold your sister's hand.
We're gonna get you out of here.

00:02:05.838 --> 00:02:07.470
Let's go, let's go.

00:02:10.938 --> 00:02:12.491
All right, go!

00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:16.683
Sam!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.480
Sam, get them out of here!

00:02:24.515 --> 00:02:25.860
Here, take this!

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.235
Run!

00:02:37.255 --> 00:02:39.663
Come on!

00:03:17.972 --> 00:03:19.491
Dean!

00:03:20.268 --> 00:03:21.147
Dean!

00:03:21.368 --> 00:03:22.256
Hey!

00:03:22.693 --> 00:03:24.599
Hey, hey!

00:03:34.211 --> 00:03:35.742
Sorry, I'm so sorry to ask.

00:03:35.777 --> 00:03:38.115
There doesn't seem to
be any insurance on file.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.157
Right, um...

00:03:41.869 --> 00:03:43.405
Okay.

00:03:44.865 --> 00:03:48.176
Okay, Mr. Burkevits.

00:03:50.649 --> 00:03:54.279
Look, we can finish this
up later. No, no it's okay.

00:03:54.314 --> 00:03:57.286
We were just taking a short cut
through the neighborhood and um...

00:03:57.321 --> 00:04:00.073
Windows were all down,
we heard some screaming.

00:04:00.108 --> 00:04:02.826
We drove pass the house
and we stopped, ran in.

00:04:02.861 --> 00:04:04.356
And you found the kids in the basement.

00:04:04.391 --> 00:04:05.227
Yeah.

00:04:05.262 --> 00:04:07.508
Well, thank god you did.

00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:11.045
Excuse me. Sure, thanks for your help.

00:04:11.311 --> 00:04:12.256
Hey, doc. Is he...

00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:14.428
He's resting. And?

00:04:14.463 --> 00:04:16.953
The electrocution
triggered a heart attack.

00:04:16.988 --> 00:04:21.709
A pretty massive one. I'm
afraid his heart, it's damaged.

00:04:21.744 --> 00:04:24.386
How damaged? We've done all we can.

00:04:24.421 --> 00:04:27.643
We can try and keep him
comfortable at this point but...

00:04:27.678 --> 00:04:30.866
I'll give him a couple of
weeks at most, maybe a month.

00:04:30.901 --> 00:04:32.397
No, no, there is...

00:04:32.432 --> 00:04:35.278
There's gotta be something you
can do. Some kind of treatment.

00:04:35.313 --> 00:04:37.522
We can't work miracles.

00:04:37.557 --> 00:04:40.200
I really am sorry.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:55.107
You ever actually watched
daytime TV? It's terrible.

00:04:56.757 --> 00:04:58.342
I talked to your doctor.

00:04:58.377 --> 00:05:00.790
That fabric soft teddy bear, oh.

00:05:00.825 --> 00:05:03.699
I'll hunt that bitch down. Dean...

00:05:03.734 --> 00:05:05.947
Yeah.

00:05:05.982 --> 00:05:09.743
All right, well. Looks like
you're gonna leave town without me.

00:05:09.778 --> 00:05:11.808
What are you talking about?
I'm not gonna leave you here.

00:05:11.843 --> 00:05:13.713
Hey, if you take care of that car.

00:05:13.748 --> 00:05:15.549
I'll swear I'll hunt your ass.

00:05:15.584 --> 00:05:19.551
I don't think that's funny. Uh,
come on. It's a little funny.

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:29.528
Look, Sam. What can I say,
man. It's a dangerous gig.

00:05:29.563 --> 00:05:31.976
I drew the short straw.
That it, end of story.

00:05:32.011 --> 00:05:34.254
Don't talk like that, all right?

00:05:34.289 --> 00:05:37.256
We still have options. What options?

00:05:37.291 --> 00:05:40.154
Get burial or cremation?

00:05:40.189 --> 00:05:43.017
I know it's not easy.

00:05:44.165 --> 00:05:46.788
But I'm gonna die.

00:05:46.968 --> 00:05:49.702
And you can't stop it.

00:05:51.695 --> 00:05:53.436
Watch me.

00:05:53.471 --> 00:05:55.935
This is John Winchester.
I can't be reached.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.399
If this is an emergency
call my son Dean.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:03.702
866-907-3235.
He can help.

00:06:03.737 --> 00:06:06.474
Hey, dad. It's Sam.

00:06:07.745 --> 00:06:10.111
You probably won't get this but uh...

00:06:10.146 --> 00:06:12.064
It's Dean...

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:14.803
He's sick and uh...

00:06:14.967 --> 00:06:18.588
Doctors says there
nothing they can do. Um...

00:06:19.874 --> 00:06:21.260
But uh...

00:06:21.295 --> 00:06:24.278
They don't know things
we know, right? Um...

00:06:24.313 --> 00:06:26.942
So, don't worry, cause I'm uh...

00:06:26.977 --> 00:06:30.066
Gonna do everything it
takes to get him better.

00:06:30.982 --> 00:06:32.460
All right.

00:06:32.495 --> 00:06:34.868
Just wanted you to know.

00:06:49.482 --> 00:06:50.811
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:50.846 --> 00:06:53.818
I checked myself out. Are you crazy?

00:06:53.853 --> 00:06:57.896
I'm not gonna die in a hospital
where the nurses aren't even hot.

00:06:58.139 --> 00:07:00.407
You know, this whole...

00:07:00.442 --> 00:07:02.874
I laugh in the face of
death thing... It's crap.

00:07:02.909 --> 00:07:05.199
I can see right through it.

00:07:05.234 --> 00:07:07.158
Yeah, whatever dude.

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:09.389
Have you even slept?
You look worse than me.

00:07:09.424 --> 00:07:13.160
I've been scattering the
internet for the last three days.

00:07:14.737 --> 00:07:17.780
Calling every contact
in dad journal. For what?

00:07:17.815 --> 00:07:19.608
For what'll help you.

00:07:19.643 --> 00:07:22.699
One of dad's friends
Joshua. He called me back.

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:25.271
Told me about a guy in
Nebraska. Specialist.

00:07:25.306 --> 00:07:27.808
You're not gonna let me
die in peace, are you?

00:07:27.843 --> 00:07:29.861
I'm not gonna let you die, period.

00:07:29.896 --> 00:07:32.380
We're going.

00:07:52.525 --> 00:07:55.642
The church of Roy Le Grange
Faith Healer. Witness the miracle

00:07:56.945 --> 00:07:59.899
I got you. I got it!

00:08:00.824 --> 00:08:02.756
Man, you're a lying bastard.

00:08:02.791 --> 00:08:04.855
I thought you said we
were going to see a doctor.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:06.578
I believe I said a 'specialist'.

00:08:06.613 --> 00:08:08.852
Look Dean, this guy's
suppose to be the real deal.

00:08:08.887 --> 00:08:12.322
I can't believe you brought me here to see
some guy who heals people out of a tent!

00:08:12.357 --> 00:08:15.336
Reverend Le Grange is a
great man. Yeah, that's nice.

00:08:15.371 --> 00:08:17.591
I have a right to protest.
This man is a fraud.

00:08:17.626 --> 00:08:20.074
He's bilking all these people
out of their hard earned money!

00:08:20.109 --> 00:08:23.513
This is a place of
worship. Let's go, move it.

00:08:23.548 --> 00:08:25.755
I take it he's not part of the flock.

00:08:25.790 --> 00:08:28.176
What would people see something
that they can't explain.

00:08:28.211 --> 00:08:30.563
There's controversy. Come
on, Sam. A Faith Healer?

00:08:30.598 --> 00:08:33.913
Maybe it's time to have
a little faith Dean.

00:08:34.666 --> 00:08:36.733
You know what I got faith in? Reality.

00:08:36.768 --> 00:08:38.966
Knowing what's really going on.

00:08:39.001 --> 00:08:40.548
How can you be a skeptic?

00:08:40.583 --> 00:08:42.010
With the things we see everyday.

00:08:42.045 --> 00:08:44.021
Exactly, we see them.
We know they're real.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:45.319
But if you know evil's out there

00:08:45.354 --> 00:08:46.920
How can you not believe
good's out there too?

00:08:46.955 --> 00:08:48.486
Cause I've seen what
evil does to good people.

00:08:48.521 --> 00:08:51.307
Maybe god works in mysterious ways.

00:08:51.868 --> 00:08:53.950
Maybe he does.

00:08:53.985 --> 00:08:56.265
I think you just turned
me Around on the subject.

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:58.349
Yeah, I'm sure.

00:08:58.384 --> 00:09:00.477
I'm Dean. This is Sam.

00:09:00.512 --> 00:09:02.249
Leila.

00:09:02.284 --> 00:09:05.645
Sir, if you're not a believer
then why are you here?

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:09.156
Well, apparently my brother here
believes enough for the both of us.

00:09:09.191 --> 00:09:12.446
Come on Leila. It's
about to start. All right.

00:09:12.481 --> 00:09:14.216
Bye.

00:09:14.483 --> 00:09:17.433
Well, I bet you, she can
work in mysterious ways.

00:09:17.468 --> 00:09:19.561
Ladies and gentlemen, please be seated.

00:09:19.596 --> 00:09:22.889
We're starting in just a moment.
Welcome all faiths True believers revival

00:09:25.204 --> 00:09:28.506
Yeah, peace love and trust all over.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.222
Come on.

00:09:34.257 --> 00:09:35.561
Don't, we're sitting here.

00:09:35.596 --> 00:09:36.998
We're sitting up front.

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:38.400
What? Why? Come on.

00:09:38.435 --> 00:09:39.927
Oh, come on Sam.

00:09:39.962 --> 00:09:41.384
You're all right?

00:09:41.419 --> 00:09:45.086
This is ridiculous. I'm
good, dude. Get off me.

00:09:46.113 --> 00:09:48.096
Perfect. Yeah, perfect.

00:09:48.131 --> 00:09:50.064
Take it off

00:09:59.786 --> 00:10:04.388
Each morning my wife Sue
Ann brings me the news.

00:10:04.423 --> 00:10:06.939
Never seems good, does it? No.

00:10:06.974 --> 00:10:09.421
Seems like there's always someone

00:10:09.456 --> 00:10:14.863
Committing some immoral,
unspeakable act. That's right.

00:10:14.898 --> 00:10:17.989
But I say to you. God is watching.

00:10:18.024 --> 00:10:19.434
Here, here.

00:10:19.469 --> 00:10:25.987
God rewards the good and he
punishes the corrupt. Right.

00:10:26.022 --> 00:10:30.614
It is the Lord who does
the healing here friends.

00:10:30.649 --> 00:10:35.172
The Lord who guides me
and chosen who to heal

00:10:35.207 --> 00:10:38.788
By helping me to see into
people's hearts. Amen.

00:10:38.823 --> 00:10:41.233
Yeah, rid of their wallets.

00:10:41.268 --> 00:10:43.643
You think so young man?

00:10:45.084 --> 00:10:48.503
Sorry. No, no. Don't be.

00:10:48.538 --> 00:10:53.479
Just watch what you say around a
blind man. We got real sharp ears.

00:10:54.535 --> 00:10:56.929
What's your name son?

00:10:57.567 --> 00:11:00.342
Dean. Dean.

00:11:02.083 --> 00:11:05.871
I want you to come up here with me.

00:11:12.830 --> 00:11:15.402
No, it's okay.

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:16.690
What are you doing?

00:11:16.725 --> 00:11:20.618
You come here to be healed, haven't you?

00:11:22.829 --> 00:11:25.647
Oh, yeah but uh...

00:11:25.682 --> 00:11:29.623
Maybe you should just pick someone else.

00:11:32.123 --> 00:11:36.743
I didn't pick you Dean. The Lord did.

00:11:38.224 --> 00:11:40.622
Get up there!

00:11:40.851 --> 00:11:44.994
Yes. Yes. Amen.

00:11:51.236 --> 00:11:52.962
You're ready?

00:11:52.997 --> 00:11:55.800
Yeah, with no disrespect but uh...

00:11:55.835 --> 00:11:58.623
I'm not exactly a believer.

00:11:58.768 --> 00:12:00.653
You will be son.

00:12:00.688 --> 00:12:02.538
You will be.

00:12:02.722 --> 00:12:05.396
Pray with me friends.

00:12:29.068 --> 00:12:33.260
All right now.

00:12:42.258 --> 00:12:44.862
All right now.

00:12:49.311 --> 00:12:51.028
Dean!

00:12:55.885 --> 00:12:57.925
Say something!

00:13:11.256 --> 00:13:13.111
So you really feel okay?

00:13:13.146 --> 00:13:14.464
I feel fine Sam.

00:13:14.499 --> 00:13:18.361
Well, according to all your tests.
There's nothing wrong with your heart.

00:13:18.396 --> 00:13:20.121
No sign there ever was.

00:13:20.156 --> 00:13:23.888
Not that a man your age should
be having heart trouble but uh...

00:13:23.923 --> 00:13:25.902
Still it's strange, it does happen.

00:13:25.937 --> 00:13:27.063
What do you mean strange?

00:13:27.098 --> 00:13:30.711
Well, just yesterday a young
guy like you. 27, athletic.

00:13:30.746 --> 00:13:33.414
I don't know a heart attack.

00:13:34.255 --> 00:13:36.053
Thanks doc.

00:13:36.088 --> 00:13:37.851
No problem.

00:13:39.006 --> 00:13:41.112
That's odd. Maybe it's coincidence.

00:13:41.147 --> 00:13:43.267
People's heart give up all
the time, man. No they don't.

00:13:43.302 --> 00:13:45.352
Look Dean. Do we really have
to look this one in the mouth?

00:13:45.387 --> 00:13:48.021
Why can't we just be thankful that
the guy saved your life and move on?

00:13:48.056 --> 00:13:50.787
Because I can't shake
this feeling, that's why.

00:13:50.822 --> 00:13:52.739
What feeling?

00:13:52.774 --> 00:13:56.204
When I was healed. I just, I felt wrong.

00:13:56.239 --> 00:13:59.510
Felt cold and for a second

00:13:59.545 --> 00:14:01.429
I saw someone. I saw this old man.

00:14:01.464 --> 00:14:03.278
I'm telling you Sam. It was a spirit.

00:14:03.313 --> 00:14:05.922
But if there was something there
Dean. I think I would have seen it too.

00:14:05.957 --> 00:14:08.150
I mean I've been seeing
awful lot of things lately.

00:14:08.185 --> 00:14:09.899
Well, excuse me psychic wonder.

00:14:09.934 --> 00:14:12.865
But you just need a
little faith on this one.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:17.042
Sam, I've been hunting long enough
to trust a feeling like this.

00:14:19.347 --> 00:14:21.334
Yeah, right.

00:14:22.406 --> 00:14:24.649
So what do you want to do?

00:14:24.684 --> 00:14:26.061
Why don't you to check
out that heart attack guy.

00:14:26.096 --> 00:14:28.292
I'm gonna visit the reverend.

00:14:31.221 --> 00:14:32.814
I feel great.

00:14:32.849 --> 00:14:34.372
Just trying to...

00:14:34.407 --> 00:14:36.488
You know, make sense of what happened.

00:14:36.523 --> 00:14:39.415
A miracle's what happened.

00:14:39.794 --> 00:14:44.321
Miracles come so often around Roy.

00:14:45.014 --> 00:14:47.623
When did they start? The miracles.

00:14:47.658 --> 00:14:50.197
Woke up one morning stone blind.

00:14:50.232 --> 00:14:54.564
Doctors figured out I had cancer.
Told me I had maybe a month.

00:14:54.599 --> 00:14:56.157
So uh...

00:14:56.192 --> 00:14:58.448
We prayed for a miracle.

00:14:58.483 --> 00:15:01.063
I was weak but...

00:15:01.098 --> 00:15:04.492
I told Sue Ann to just keep on praying.

00:15:04.527 --> 00:15:06.064
I went into a coma.

00:15:06.099 --> 00:15:08.898
Doctors said I wouldn't
wake up but I did.

00:15:08.933 --> 00:15:11.398
And the cancer was gone.

00:15:11.433 --> 00:15:17.095
If it wasn't for these eyes, no
one would believe I ever had it.

00:15:17.130 --> 00:15:19.804
And suddenly you can heal people?

00:15:19.839 --> 00:15:22.412
I discovered it afterwards, yes.

00:15:22.447 --> 00:15:24.950
God's blessed me in many ways.

00:15:24.985 --> 00:15:30.520
And his flock swelled over night.
And this is just the beginning.

00:15:32.156 --> 00:15:34.372
Can I ask you one last question?

00:15:34.407 --> 00:15:36.641
Of course you can.

00:15:37.333 --> 00:15:39.893
Why? Why me?

00:15:39.928 --> 00:15:43.279
Out of all the sick people why save me?

00:15:43.314 --> 00:15:47.090
Well, like I said before.
The Lord guides me.

00:15:47.125 --> 00:15:54.541
I looked into your heart and you
just stood out from all the rest.

00:15:54.705 --> 00:15:58.332
What did you see in my heart?

00:15:58.367 --> 00:16:02.126
A young man with an important
purpose. A job to do.

00:16:02.161 --> 00:16:05.183
And it isn't finished.

00:16:06.908 --> 00:16:11.003
He seemed healthy. Swam
everyday. Didn't smoke.

00:16:11.038 --> 00:16:13.899
It's no so hard to act this
kind of scene. No bizarre.

00:16:13.934 --> 00:16:16.760
And you said he was running?
Right before he collapsed?

00:16:16.795 --> 00:16:18.672
Yeah, yeah. He was freaking out.

00:16:18.707 --> 00:16:20.418
Said that something was...

00:16:20.453 --> 00:16:22.095
After him. Did he say what?

00:16:22.130 --> 00:16:25.783
Thin air, that's what. I
mean, there wasn't anything.

00:16:25.967 --> 00:16:27.854
All right, thanks.

00:16:30.309 --> 00:16:31.783
Hey buddy. You're...

00:16:31.818 --> 00:16:33.291
You're clock's busted.

00:16:33.326 --> 00:16:34.730
Oh, yeah. We uh...

00:16:34.765 --> 00:16:39.236
We can't get it working.
Just froze at 4:17.

00:16:39.271 --> 00:16:41.839
Is that the same time Marshall died?

00:16:41.874 --> 00:16:43.731
How did you know?

00:16:47.209 --> 00:16:49.756
Dean, hey. Hey.

00:16:49.953 --> 00:16:51.659
How you feeling? I feel good.

00:16:51.694 --> 00:16:54.091
Cured, I guess.

00:16:54.126 --> 00:16:55.689
What are you doing here?

00:16:55.724 --> 00:16:58.953
You know my mom. She wanted
to talk to the reverend.

00:16:58.988 --> 00:17:00.704
Leila.

00:17:01.738 --> 00:17:05.858
Yes, we're here again. Oh,
I'm sorry but Roy's resting.

00:17:05.893 --> 00:17:08.284
He won't be seeing anyone right now.

00:17:08.319 --> 00:17:10.320
Sue Ann please.

00:17:10.355 --> 00:17:12.998
This is our sixth time.
He's got to see us.

00:17:13.033 --> 00:17:15.213
Roy is aware of Leila's situation

00:17:15.248 --> 00:17:18.367
And he very well much wants to help
just as soon as the Lord allows.

00:17:18.402 --> 00:17:21.694
Have faith Mrs. Roke.

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.413
Why are you still even here?

00:17:31.448 --> 00:17:33.502
You've got what you wanted. Mom.

00:17:33.537 --> 00:17:35.365
Stop.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.976
No Leila this is too much.

00:17:38.011 --> 00:17:40.491
We've been to every single service.

00:17:40.526 --> 00:17:43.441
If Roy would stop choosing
these strangers over you.

00:17:43.476 --> 00:17:46.639
Strangers who don't even believe.

00:17:46.674 --> 00:17:49.802
I just can't pray any harder.

00:17:49.837 --> 00:17:52.448
Leila, what's wrong?

00:17:54.652 --> 00:17:56.944
I have this thing.

00:17:56.979 --> 00:17:59.236
It's a brain tumor.

00:17:59.691 --> 00:18:02.636
It's inoperable.

00:18:02.812 --> 00:18:06.547
In sixth months the doctors say...

00:18:10.982 --> 00:18:13.217
I'm sorry.

00:18:13.751 --> 00:18:15.651
It's okay.

00:18:15.686 --> 00:18:17.666
No.

00:18:17.952 --> 00:18:20.667
It isn't.

00:18:25.865 --> 00:18:30.278
Why do you deserve to
live more than my daughter?

00:18:58.652 --> 00:19:00.991
What did you find out?

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:03.631
I'm sorry.

00:19:03.819 --> 00:19:05.010
Sorry about what?

00:19:05.045 --> 00:19:10.579
Marshall Hall died at 4:17.

00:19:10.797 --> 00:19:13.285
The exact time I was healed. Yeah.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:16.863
So, I put together a list.
Everyone Roy's healed.

00:19:16.898 --> 00:19:20.509
Six people over the past year and I
cross checked them with local obits.

00:19:20.544 --> 00:19:23.245
Every time someone was
healed someone else died.

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:24.666
And each time the victim died

00:19:24.701 --> 00:19:27.572
Of the same symptom Le Grange
was healing at the time.

00:19:27.607 --> 00:19:30.443
Someone healed a cancer,
someone else died of cancer?

00:19:30.478 --> 00:19:33.849
Somehow. Le Grange...

00:19:34.033 --> 00:19:38.226
Is trading a life for another. Hello?

00:19:39.397 --> 00:19:41.101
Wait, wait, wait. So...

00:19:41.136 --> 00:19:43.713
Marshall Hall died to save me?

00:19:43.748 --> 00:19:45.642
Dean...

00:19:45.856 --> 00:19:48.282
The guy probably would have died anyway.

00:19:48.317 --> 00:19:50.708
And someone else would have been healed.

00:19:52.862 --> 00:19:55.230
You never should have brought me here.

00:19:55.265 --> 00:19:57.814
Dean, I was just trying
to save your life.

00:19:57.849 --> 00:20:00.363
But Sam, some guy is
dead now because of me!

00:20:00.398 --> 00:20:03.172
I didn't know.

00:20:04.008 --> 00:20:07.015
Pray with me friends.

00:20:07.857 --> 00:20:11.046
The thing I don't understand
is how is Roy doing it?

00:20:11.081 --> 00:20:13.892
How's he trading a life for a life?

00:20:13.927 --> 00:20:16.674
Oh, he's not doing it.

00:20:16.819 --> 00:20:18.949
Something else is doing it for him.

00:20:18.984 --> 00:20:23.268
What do you mean? The
old man I saw on stage.

00:20:23.658 --> 00:20:25.456
I didn't want to believe
it. But deep down, I knew it.

00:20:25.491 --> 00:20:27.549
You knew what? What
are you talking about?

00:20:27.584 --> 00:20:31.946
There's only one thing that can
give and take life like that.

00:20:31.981 --> 00:20:34.613
We're dealing with a reaper.

00:21:34.521 --> 00:21:36.282
You really think it's the 'Grim Reaper'?

00:21:36.317 --> 00:21:39.303
Like Angel of Death, the
Collector of Soul the whole deal?

00:21:39.338 --> 00:21:41.829
No, no, no. Not 'The
Reaper'. A 'Reaper'.

00:21:41.864 --> 00:21:44.180
There's reaper law in pretty
much every culture on earth.

00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:45.949
They go by a hundred different names.

00:21:45.984 --> 00:21:47.932
It's possible this one's one of them.

00:21:47.967 --> 00:21:49.845
But you said you saw a dude in a suit.

00:21:49.880 --> 00:21:53.845
What? You think he should be
working the whole black robe thing?

00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:56.731
You said it yourself that
the clock stopped right?

00:21:57.635 --> 00:21:59.669
Reapers stop time.

00:21:59.704 --> 00:22:01.190
And you can only see them
when they're coming at you

00:22:01.225 --> 00:22:03.247
Which is why I could
see him and you couldn't.

00:22:03.282 --> 00:22:05.234
Maybe. There's nothing
else that could be Sam.

00:22:05.269 --> 00:22:08.499
The question is how's Roy
controlling the damn thing.

00:22:08.534 --> 00:22:10.190
That cross.

00:22:10.225 --> 00:22:12.624
What? There was this cross.

00:22:12.659 --> 00:22:17.236
I noticed it in the church
tent, I knew I seen it before.

00:22:22.961 --> 00:22:24.812
Here.

00:22:25.356 --> 00:22:26.461
Tarot?

00:22:26.496 --> 00:22:28.046
It makes sense.

00:22:28.081 --> 00:22:30.232
I mean, tarot dates back to
the early Christian, right?

00:22:30.267 --> 00:22:31.998
When some priests
were still using magic?

00:22:32.033 --> 00:22:33.694
And a few of them viewed
into the dark stuff.

00:22:33.729 --> 00:22:37.905
Necromancy and how to push
death away, how to cause it.

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:40.791
So Roy's using black
magic to bind the reaper.

00:22:40.826 --> 00:22:42.986
If he is, he's riding the whirlwind.

00:22:43.021 --> 00:22:46.942
It's like putting a dog
leash on a great white.

00:22:53.083 --> 00:22:55.826
Okay, then we stop Roy. How?

00:22:55.861 --> 00:22:56.831
You know how?

00:22:56.866 --> 00:22:58.265
Wait, what the hell are
you talking about Dean?

00:22:58.300 --> 00:23:00.113
We can't kill Roy.

00:23:00.148 --> 00:23:01.301
Sam. The guy's playing god.

00:23:01.336 --> 00:23:03.953
He's deciding who lives and who
dies. That's a monster in my books.

00:23:03.988 --> 00:23:06.853
No, we're not gonna
kill a human being Dean.

00:23:06.888 --> 00:23:08.782
We do that, we're no better than he is.

00:23:08.817 --> 00:23:11.601
Okay, so we can't kill
Roy. We can't kill death.

00:23:11.636 --> 00:23:14.684
Any bright ideas college boy?

00:23:14.975 --> 00:23:16.306
Okay, uh...

00:23:16.341 --> 00:23:18.721
If Roy's using some kind
of black spell on the reaper

00:23:18.756 --> 00:23:21.149
We gotta figure out what it is.

00:23:21.184 --> 00:23:23.713
And how to break it.

00:23:28.799 --> 00:23:32.025
Service today.

00:23:36.777 --> 00:23:39.415
If Roy's using a spell.
There might be a spell book.

00:23:39.450 --> 00:23:40.617
See if you can find it.

00:23:40.652 --> 00:23:43.481
Hurry up. Services start in 15
minutes. I'll try to stroll Roy.

00:23:43.516 --> 00:23:46.259
All right. Le Grange is
a fraud. He's no healer.

00:23:46.294 --> 00:23:47.961
Amen, brother. You
keep up the good work.

00:23:47.996 --> 00:23:49.650
Thank you.

00:24:46.478 --> 00:24:48.770
Encyclopedia of Christian
History Old & New Testament

00:25:15.334 --> 00:25:20.934
Openly gay teacher wins lawsuit
Strong message sent to Nations...

00:25:31.058 --> 00:25:34.316
Wright: 'local church a cult'

00:25:43.843 --> 00:25:44.726
What have you got?

00:25:44.761 --> 00:25:46.751
Roy's choosing victims
he sees as a immoral.

00:25:46.786 --> 00:25:48.706
And I think I know
who's next on his list.

00:25:48.741 --> 00:25:50.755
Remember the protestor?
The guy in the parking lot?

00:25:50.790 --> 00:25:52.814
Yeah. Yeah, I'll find him.

00:25:52.849 --> 00:25:55.795
But you can't let Roy
heal anyone, all right?

00:26:16.410 --> 00:26:17.346
Leila.

00:26:17.381 --> 00:26:20.606
Leila Roke, come up here child.

00:26:25.896 --> 00:26:27.898
Mom... Baby.

00:26:27.933 --> 00:26:29.900
I love you.

00:26:30.950 --> 00:26:33.042
Oh, man.

00:26:42.169 --> 00:26:44.846
Leila, listen to me.
You can't get up there.

00:26:44.881 --> 00:26:46.824
Why not? We've waited for months.

00:26:46.859 --> 00:26:48.623
You can't let Roy heal you.

00:26:48.658 --> 00:26:50.671
I don't understand. Roy
healed you, didn't he?

00:26:50.706 --> 00:26:52.649
I mean, why wouldn't
you at least let him try?

00:26:52.684 --> 00:26:55.890
Because if you do, something
bad is going to happen.

00:26:55.925 --> 00:26:59.096
I can't explain. I just need
you to believe me. Leila.

00:26:59.131 --> 00:27:01.295
Please...

00:27:09.560 --> 00:27:10.972
I'm sorry.

00:27:11.007 --> 00:27:12.875
Leila. Leila!

00:27:12.910 --> 00:27:14.743
Dear child.

00:27:15.834 --> 00:27:19.019
You deserve this. I knew
the Lord would reply me...

00:27:19.054 --> 00:27:21.952
I knew the Lord would reply me.

00:27:25.421 --> 00:27:27.286
Help!

00:27:34.366 --> 00:27:36.717
Pray with me friends.

00:27:40.804 --> 00:27:43.889
I hope you're ready. I am.

00:27:54.165 --> 00:27:55.506
Help!

00:27:55.541 --> 00:27:56.899
Help me please!

00:27:56.934 --> 00:27:58.257
Where is it?

00:27:58.472 --> 00:28:00.724
It's right there!

00:28:02.157 --> 00:28:04.169
Come on, come on.

00:28:12.920 --> 00:28:14.390
Fire!

00:28:14.425 --> 00:28:16.996
The tent's on fire!

00:28:17.144 --> 00:28:19.131
Fire! Everybody get out of here!

00:28:19.166 --> 00:28:21.716
Roy! Roy, please!

00:28:21.751 --> 00:28:23.864
Please don't stop. Please!

00:28:23.899 --> 00:28:25.840
Reverend, please!

00:28:25.875 --> 00:28:27.781
Please don't stop.

00:28:27.816 --> 00:28:29.400
Please.

00:28:29.435 --> 00:28:30.950
Friends.

00:28:30.985 --> 00:28:34.561
If you all just leave the tent
in an orderly fashion and...

00:28:34.596 --> 00:28:37.269
We'll figure out what's
going on out there and...

00:28:37.304 --> 00:28:40.161
I did it. I stopped Roy.

00:28:40.196 --> 00:28:43.018
David? I think its okay.

00:28:46.768 --> 00:28:48.378
No!

00:28:48.413 --> 00:28:49.605
Dean, it didn't work!

00:28:49.640 --> 00:28:51.626
The reaper's still coming!

00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:54.143
I'm telling you... I'm telling you.

00:28:54.178 --> 00:28:56.777
It must not have worked! Roy must
not be controlling this thing!

00:28:56.812 --> 00:28:59.305
Then who the hell is?

00:29:02.356 --> 00:29:04.469
Sue Ann.

00:29:18.611 --> 00:29:20.903
Help! Help me!

00:29:21.047 --> 00:29:22.837
Help!

00:29:37.268 --> 00:29:39.591
I got you. I got you.

00:29:42.134 --> 00:29:44.118
Thank god.

00:29:49.398 --> 00:29:52.433
I just don't understand.

00:29:52.468 --> 00:29:54.231
After everything we have done for you.

00:29:54.266 --> 00:29:57.358
After Roy healed you.

00:29:58.312 --> 00:30:02.658
I'm just very very disappointed Dean.

00:30:03.994 --> 00:30:06.467
You can let him go. I'm
not gonna press charges.

00:30:06.502 --> 00:30:11.656
The Lord will deal
with him as he sees fit.

00:30:13.401 --> 00:30:14.976
We catch you around here again son.

00:30:15.011 --> 00:30:17.727
Who put the fear god in you, understand?

00:30:17.762 --> 00:30:19.494
Yes, sir. Fear god.

00:30:19.529 --> 00:30:21.348
Got it.

00:30:24.400 --> 00:30:25.932
Leila.

00:30:26.621 --> 00:30:28.244
Why would you do that Dean?

00:30:28.279 --> 00:30:30.574
It could have been my only chance.

00:30:30.609 --> 00:30:32.551
He's not a healer.

00:30:32.586 --> 00:30:34.493
He healed you.

00:30:36.131 --> 00:30:38.174
I know it doesn't seem fair.

00:30:38.209 --> 00:30:42.808
And I wish I could explain. But
Roy's not the answer, I'm sorry.

00:30:44.787 --> 00:30:47.293
Goodbye Dean.

00:30:51.870 --> 00:30:55.839
I wish you luck. I really do.

00:30:55.874 --> 00:30:58.451
Same to you.

00:31:02.427 --> 00:31:05.721
You deserve it a lot more than me.

00:31:09.074 --> 00:31:11.539
Private session tonight.
No interruptions.

00:31:11.574 --> 00:31:14.004
I give you my word.
I'll heal your daughter.

00:31:14.039 --> 00:31:17.530
Thank you, reverend. God bless you.

00:31:21.640 --> 00:31:24.913
So Roy really believes.

00:31:25.452 --> 00:31:28.101
I don't think he has any
idea what his wife's doing.

00:31:28.136 --> 00:31:32.308
Well, I found this
Hidden in their library.

00:31:32.343 --> 00:31:35.604
It's ancient. Written by a
priest who went dark side.

00:31:35.639 --> 00:31:37.678
There's a binding spell in here.

00:31:37.713 --> 00:31:39.502
For trapping a reaper.

00:31:39.537 --> 00:31:41.889
Must be hell of a spell. Yeah.

00:31:41.924 --> 00:31:45.148
You got to build a black altar
with seriously dark stuff.

00:31:45.183 --> 00:31:48.637
Bones. Human blood.

00:31:48.672 --> 00:31:52.132
To cross a line like
that. That preacher's wife.

00:31:52.167 --> 00:31:56.676
Black magic, murder, evil.

00:31:56.711 --> 00:31:58.480
Desperate.

00:31:58.515 --> 00:32:01.788
Her husband was dying. She would
have done anything to save him.

00:32:01.823 --> 00:32:05.061
She was using the binding spell
to keep the reaper away from Roy.

00:32:05.096 --> 00:32:08.701
Cheating death. Literally.

00:32:08.736 --> 00:32:12.110
Yeah, but Roy's alive so why
is she still using the spell?

00:32:12.145 --> 00:32:17.651
Right. To force the reaper to help
the people she thinks are moral.

00:32:18.655 --> 00:32:22.116
Thank god save us from half the people
who think they're doing god's work.

00:32:22.151 --> 00:32:25.714
We got to break that binding spell Dean.

00:32:27.928 --> 00:32:30.325
You know Sue Ann had to
cop a cross like this.

00:32:30.360 --> 00:32:32.687
And when she dropped it
the reaper backed off.

00:32:32.722 --> 00:32:35.599
So you think we got to find
the cross or destroy the altar.

00:32:35.634 --> 00:32:37.578
Maybe both?

00:32:38.610 --> 00:32:41.025
Whatever we do. We'd
better to do it soon.

00:32:41.060 --> 00:32:44.021
Roy's healing Leila tonight.

00:32:55.866 --> 00:32:57.742
That's Leila's car.

00:32:57.777 --> 00:32:59.618
She's already here.

00:32:59.653 --> 00:33:01.405
Yeah.

00:33:02.166 --> 00:33:04.907
Dean. You know, if Roy would
have picked Leila instead of me.

00:33:04.942 --> 00:33:07.067
She'd be healed by now. Dean, don't.

00:33:07.102 --> 00:33:09.385
And if she's not healed tonight...

00:33:09.420 --> 00:33:11.813
She's gonna die in a couple of months.

00:33:11.848 --> 00:33:14.172
What's happening to her is horrible.

00:33:14.207 --> 00:33:18.518
But what are you going to do?
Let somebody else die to save her?

00:33:18.553 --> 00:33:23.183
You said it yourself
Dean. You can't play god.

00:33:37.034 --> 00:33:38.071
Gather around.

00:33:38.106 --> 00:33:40.259
Please, everyone gather around.

00:33:40.294 --> 00:33:42.412
Come in closer. Come on up.

00:33:42.447 --> 00:33:44.704
Where's Sue Ann?

00:33:45.129 --> 00:33:47.144
House.

00:33:47.956 --> 00:33:49.464
Go find Sue Ann. I'll catch up.

00:33:49.499 --> 00:33:50.981
What are you...

00:33:52.363 --> 00:33:54.013
Hey.

00:33:54.723 --> 00:33:58.099
You're gonna put that fear god in me?

00:34:41.751 --> 00:34:43.534
See him?

00:34:43.858 --> 00:34:45.692
Na.

00:35:06.661 --> 00:35:09.086
Psycho mutt.

00:35:54.433 --> 00:35:58.579
I gave your brother a life
and I can take it away.

00:36:10.132 --> 00:36:12.042
Sam, can't you see?

00:36:12.077 --> 00:36:13.917
The Lord chose me.

00:36:13.952 --> 00:36:16.687
The reward the just
and punish the wicked.

00:36:16.722 --> 00:36:19.070
And your brother is wicked.

00:36:19.105 --> 00:36:23.485
And he deserves to die just
as Leila deserves to live.

00:36:23.520 --> 00:36:26.219
That's god's will.

00:36:28.429 --> 00:36:30.948
Goodbye Sam.

00:36:35.014 --> 00:36:36.700
Mrs. Roke.

00:36:36.735 --> 00:36:38.909
You pray with me now.

00:36:38.944 --> 00:36:41.084
Pray with me friends.

00:37:10.225 --> 00:37:12.298
All right now.

00:37:13.361 --> 00:37:16.187
All right now.

00:37:41.927 --> 00:37:43.857
All right.

00:38:09.370 --> 00:38:14.587
I don't understand. I
don't feel different.

00:38:15.425 --> 00:38:16.495
My god!

00:38:16.530 --> 00:38:18.449
What have you done?

00:38:18.484 --> 00:38:20.368
He's not your god.

00:38:20.403 --> 00:38:22.407
Reverend?

00:38:22.442 --> 00:38:24.412
Sue Ann?

00:39:10.727 --> 00:39:12.444
You okay?

00:39:12.732 --> 00:39:14.801
A little bit weak.

00:39:14.836 --> 00:39:16.472
Yeah.

00:39:17.674 --> 00:39:19.534
All right, come on.

00:39:19.569 --> 00:39:21.394
We should get going.

00:39:32.740 --> 00:39:34.834
What is it?

00:39:34.869 --> 00:39:36.928
Nothing.

00:39:38.307 --> 00:39:39.585
What is it?

00:39:39.620 --> 00:39:41.550
We did the right thing here, didn't' we?

00:39:41.585 --> 00:39:43.618
Of course we did.

00:39:43.653 --> 00:39:45.975
I didn't feel like it.

00:39:47.073 --> 00:39:48.784
I got it.

00:39:52.610 --> 00:39:56.005
Leila, come on in. Hey.

00:39:56.040 --> 00:39:57.916
Hey.

00:39:58.762 --> 00:40:00.570
How did you know we were here?

00:40:00.605 --> 00:40:02.461
Sam called.

00:40:02.496 --> 00:40:06.242
He said you wanted to say goodbye.

00:40:06.409 --> 00:40:09.423
I'm gonna grab a soda.

00:40:14.143 --> 00:40:16.268
So um...

00:40:16.303 --> 00:40:19.484
Where are you going?

00:40:19.519 --> 00:40:20.690
Don't know yet.

00:40:20.725 --> 00:40:24.769
Our work kind of takes us all over so...

00:40:26.499 --> 00:40:30.863
You know, I went back to see Roy.

00:40:30.898 --> 00:40:33.527
What happened?

00:40:34.756 --> 00:40:37.068
Nothing.

00:40:37.290 --> 00:40:43.313
He laid his hand on my
forehead. But nothing happened.

00:40:43.348 --> 00:40:45.907
I'm sorry.

00:40:46.091 --> 00:40:48.670
I'm sorry it didn't work.

00:40:48.705 --> 00:40:50.642
And Sue Ann...

00:40:50.677 --> 00:40:52.342
She's dead, you know?

00:40:52.377 --> 00:40:54.292
A stroke.

00:40:54.327 --> 00:40:57.411
Yeah, I heard.

00:40:58.068 --> 00:41:01.210
Yeah, Roy's a good man.

00:41:01.383 --> 00:41:04.614
He doesn't deserve what's happened.

00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:09.845
Must be ruff...

00:41:09.880 --> 00:41:12.250
To believe in something so much.

00:41:12.285 --> 00:41:15.665
And have it disappoint you like that.

00:41:19.801 --> 00:41:23.103
You want to hear something weird?

00:41:24.304 --> 00:41:29.131
I'm okay. Really.

00:41:29.166 --> 00:41:31.525
I guess if you're gonna have faith

00:41:31.560 --> 00:41:34.703
We can't just have it
when the miracles happen.

00:41:34.738 --> 00:41:39.978
You have to have it when they don't.

00:41:44.628 --> 00:41:48.077
So what now?

00:41:50.489 --> 00:41:54.977
God works in mysterious ways.

00:41:59.107 --> 00:42:01.479
Goodbye Dean.

00:42:03.207 --> 00:42:04.923
Hey.

00:42:10.176 --> 00:42:15.269
I'm not much of a praying type but...

00:42:16.137 --> 00:42:19.611
I'm gonna pray for you.

00:42:20.769 --> 00:42:23.118
Well...

00:42:23.284 --> 00:42:26.769
There's a miracle right there.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
